        "Array"
      ],
      "required": false,
      "hasFactoryDefault": false,
      "control": "text",
      "description": "`grid-template-areas`. Two accepted shapes:\n\n- `string[]` — every entry is one row of the template\n  (`['header header', 'sidebar main']`). Each entry is wrapped in\n  quotes by the component, so the consumer doesn't have to.\n- `string` — raw CSS, passed verbatim. Use it when you want to\n  inline `\". header .\"` style escape hatches with multiple double-\n  quoted rows yourself.",
      "source": "types"
    },
    {
      "name": "autoFlow",
      "label": "autoFlow",
